{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>The name of the one was Gershom, etc.</b> It was necessary to write the reason for the name a second time, after having already written it in the portion of Shemot (Exodus 2:22), so that you should know that this is the one spoken of in the portion of Shemot and not another who happened to be called by the same name." "<b>Further,</b> perhaps the verse was concerned that a person might say that the reason he named him Gershom was because Jethro had driven him away from his table or from his house. And although he stated the reason ״גֵּר הָיִיתִי״ etc., perhaps he said this only because he did not want Jethro to feel offended — therefore the verse repeated and justified the matter even at a time when there was no concern for Jethro's feelings, for the reason of the <b>name</b> etc. is <b>כִּי אָמַר</b> (for he said) etc. And the explanation of the meaning of ״כִּי אָמַר גֵּר״ etc. I have already explained in the portion of Shemot (Exodus 2:22)."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:29:22.544029657Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}